# This repository is developed on Windows and deployed on Linux.
#
# A shell script checked out with CRLF fails inside a container with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M" — a message that names neither the file nor the
# real cause. These stay LF on every platform.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.dockerfile    text eol=lf
docker/*.conf   text eol=lf

# The SQL that carries the constraints and the audit trigger is applied by
# splitting on statement boundaries; keeping it LF keeps that deterministic.
*.sql           text eol=lf
